        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>Right guard soldier – Detail\nThe noble soldier guarding the tomb's entrance wears kausias (Macedonian flat hat), short chitons, Macedonian chlamydes  and boots, and hold sarrissas (long speares or pikes); he is in tears. \nA moving representation depicts two full-length young men wrapped in long chlamyses standing sorrowful next to the tomb's entrance, eternal guards of their dead fellow warrior. These two figures constitute the finest examples of Macedonian painting found so far; their style can be readily compared to Florentine mannerism. \n</p><p>Macedonian Tomb \n325 – 300 BC\n</p>\nAgios Athanosios, Thessaloniki, Greece",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
